// `src/hir/hir.npk` — THE HIGH-LEVEL INTERMEDIATE'S LAYER ENTRY. A module above `hir`
// writes one import, this file, and reaches what the layer offers.
//
// FILLED BY cycle 0.2, governed by `meta/specs/HIR.md`. Desugaring and normalisation,
// flattened into a POD arena: a node declares no owning field, which is why `HIR.md` H-2
// keeps a group's name as an offset into a `Bytes` rather than as an owned string. That is
// H-2's design, and a `Vec` of nodes MUST keep it (`SAFETY.md` S-23a, RX-155) -- and since
// `Vec<T: Copy>` (RX-188) the compiler keeps it too, at the type.
//
// SINCE CYCLE 0.2.0 THE LAYER HOLDS THE ARENA AND ITS TEXT: `repr.npk`, the nine kinds and
// the arena (RX-223, RX-224), and `dump.npk`, the HIR as one line of text and back (RX-225),
// with `ClassRange` from `unicode` (RX-222). SINCE CYCLE 0.2.1 `build.npk` BUILDS A HIR FROM A
// PATTERN'S AST, H-5's table and nothing else, and stops at its hooks or in `leaf` until cycle
// 0.3.4 (RX-228). SINCE CYCLE 0.2.2 IT REFUSES A PATTERN WHOSE NESTED REPETITIONS MULTIPLY PAST
// `NREGEX_REPEAT_PRODUCT`, on the way down, and `hir_build_refusal` is the refusal (RX-232).
//
// EVERY LINE BELOW IS `pub use`, ONE NAME PER LINE (`BUILD.md` B-15a rules 1 and 3).
//
// LAYERING (`BUILD.md` §6, rule B-16). May import: `syntax`, `unicode`, `core`. A program
// importing this file owes `core`'s eleven arms.
mod:hir;

// ---- a class's ranges, `unicode`'s type (RX-222) -- re-exported, because the oracle may
// import `core` and `hir` and nothing else (B-17), and it reads every class's ranges -------
pub use "../unicode/unicode.npk".ClassRange;

